WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.834
-We are so luck to have
our friend, Fred Armisen,

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.234
leading the band all the week.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.367
It's great to see you, Fred.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:08.734
-Hi.
-It's so fun to have you here,

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.400
because you can always keep me
up to date

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.934
on your other projects.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:13.334
But this one, I had to see,

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.400
because you've sort of been
doing a bit of a press tour.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.701
I saw you on
"Good Morning America",

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.934
I saw you on NBC's very own
"Today Show",

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.033
announcing that you have
a competing holiday

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:25.234
with Valentine's Day
that you're starting this year.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.300
-That's right.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:31.434
-We would love -- I think we
would all love to hear about it.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.033
-It's called Acquaintance Day.
-Okay.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.767
-So we're just celebrating
people that you know

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.534
kind of well, you know, you see
them once in a while

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.100
every couple of years.
-Okay.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.567
-And those are really important
relationships --

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.133
you know, people you don't know
their last names,

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.267
but you just recognize
their face.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:50.534
And it's just a celebration,
so, you know,

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.934
we're just trying to find a way
for people to send cards --

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:55.334
find their address first
then send the card.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.767
-Right, I would imagine finding
an address is difficult

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.734
if you don't know
a person's last name.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:03.167
-It's difficult, but at the same
time, that's the fun of it.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.067
You know, it's that exploration
of, like, trying to find

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.667
that person -- "Oh, there you
are, you know.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.300
Let's celebrate
Acquaintance Day."

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.601
-And now what -- wait.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.667
So, example, if Hallmark made
an Acquaintance Day card

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.567
and I open it up,
what would it say inside,

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:17.133
like, what's the sort of
the text on those?

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.501
-"Remember the time we saw
each other?

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.534
Those times are always great.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.234
The times that we saw
each other's faces

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:24.834
we'll always, always remember.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:29.434
You're special to me
once every two years.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.601
Thinking of you
this whole week."

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:32.968
It's that kind of thing.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:33.968
-That's really good.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.334
I'm so excited --
Acquaintance Day.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:38.968
Look out, Valentine's Day,
a-look out.

